# CodeQL false-positive baseline -- local ai-review / reviewdrain codeql-python path.
# Consumed by codeql-review --baseline (auto-attached when this file is present);
# format matches codeql-sarif-fingerprints.py / codeql-sarif-filter.py:
#   <ruleId>\t<repo-relative-path>\t<primaryLocationLineHash>:<version>
# Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
#
# ONE entry, a genuine false positive:
# - tor_status.py write_to_temp_then_move() prints content via redact_credentials(),
#   which masks every credential option (Socks5ProxyPassword, *ProxyAuthenticator,
#   HashedControlPassword, Bridge, ...) to [REDACTED] before the print; CodeQL does
#   not recognize the sanitizer, so it reports a clear-text-logging finding here.
#
# The clear-text-STORAGE finding that CodeQL previously reported at the staging
# write is no longer present: the staging file is now created 0600 (O_NOFOLLOW) in
# a root:user 0770 directory and the final torrc is 0640 root:debian-tor, so the
# plaintext proxy credential Tor requires is not readable by any other local
# account. Nothing is suppressed for it.
py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data	usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/tor_control_panel/tor_status.py	91900677974e2eb:1
